{
  "version": 1,
  "readme": [
    "pianoroll-shared \u2014 one part, several instruments.",
    "",
    "`chords` and `bass` are pianoroll modulators: note patterns that belong to",
    "no track. `chords` is patched into BOTH `keys` (a karplus pluck) and `pad`",
    "(tapepad) \u2014 edit it once and both follow. `bass` plays `sub`. `drums` keeps",
    "its own pattern on the track itself, like any track can.",
    "",
    "In lilypad: click a node's mini roll (or 'piano roll\u2026' in the inspector) to",
    "edit a pattern. On `drums` the rows are its sample slots, not pitches.",
    "",
    "Try:",
    "  /start",
    "  /chords events              the pattern, as a list and as one line",
    "  /chords length=6            a 6-beat roll against the 8-beat loop",
    "  /unpatch id=<x> \u2026           take the pad off the chords (see /patches)",
    "  /bass velocity=0.5 4b       the roll's own fader"
  ],
